=== SURVIVOR ANALYSIS (both proven subsumed, neither a bypass) ===

R05 widen migration.go:202 disclosure vocabulary by one member ("broadcast_everything").
Probe drove the real Migrate entry with the widened build:
  PROBE err=configuration migration encode target failed sourceUnchanged=true backups=[] staging=[]
The widened value is still refused downstream by validation.go:552 during the
EncodeCurrent round trip, and that clause is itself pinned by refusal_test.go
"directory summary choice". Source unchanged, no backup written, no
.ax-config-* staging leak. Fail-closed; not an admitted-what-must-be-rejected.

R17b widen writer.go encodeVersion2 default branch to pass any backend id through.
Site carries config-refusal-subsumed and the justification holds: Migrate reaches
encodeVersion2 only from a Configuration 1.0.0 source (v2->v2 short-circuits,
v3->v2 is ErrMigrationDowngrade), validateLegacyTerminalBackend (validation.go:225)
admits only "tmux"/"conpty", and translateLegacyTerminal (validation.go:209) maps
those to ax.tmux/ax.conpty. The default branch is unreachable from production.

